  "description": "Reid Quest 2 SO eBike | Electric bike\nPowerful, comfortable and ready for new adventures – an electric bike designed for confident commuting, leisure rides and exploring light trails.\nThe Reid Quest 2 SO eBike combines smooth mid-drive electric assistance with a lightweight alloy frame and quality components, making it a versatile choice for everyday journeys, longer rides and exploring varied terrain.\nIts lightweight alloy frame features internal cable routing and an integrated 36V 417Wh battery, creating a clean, streamlined design with balanced handling. An Ananda 250W mid-motor delivers natural-feeling electric assistance to support everyday riding and help tackle hills and longer distances. The Ananda D18 Bluetooth display keeps essential ride information within easy reach and offers app compatibility.\nThe Uding D5 suspension fork provides 100mm of travel with hydraulic lockout, helping absorb bumps and vibrations across uneven surfaces while allowing riders to lock the suspension when a firmer setup is preferred.\nA Shimano 9-speed drivetrain, combining a trigger shifter and rear derailleur with an 11-46T cassette, provides a wide gear range for tackling varied gradients. The Ananda 38T chainset completes the gearing setup, while Tektro hydraulic disc brakes with 180mm rotors deliver dependable stopping power and controlled braking.\nKenda 27.5 x 2.35-inch tyres offer grip, stability and comfort across urban roads, cycle paths and light trails. Completing the setup are 640mm alloy riser handlebars, an adjustable 85mm stem, a Comfort Plus saddle and ergonomic lock-on grips, creating a relaxed and supportive riding position.\nThe Quest 2 SO eBike is ideal for:\n\nEveryday commuters, with smooth electric assistance for regular journeys\n\nRiders tackling hills and longer distances, with an Ananda 250W mid-motor\n\nLeisure and weekend cycling, with a comfortable setup for exploring further afield\n\nLight trail exploration, with a 100mm Uding D5 suspension fork and grippy Kenda tyres\n\nRiders wanting versatile gearing, with a Shimano 9-speed drivetrain and wide-range 11-46T cassette\n\nRiders who value reliable braking, with Tektro hydraulic disc brakes and 180mm rotors\n\nComfort-focused cyclists, with 640mm riser handlebars, an adjustable stem and ergonomic lock-on grips\n\nPlease make sure to familiarise yourself with eBike safety information before charging or using your new Reid. You can view and download user manuals and safety instructions here.",
